Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.17,0:00:33.04,Italics,Eren,0,0,0,,I won't cry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.65,0:00:36.72,Italics,Eren,0,0,0,,I can't be the one crying...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.23,0:00:39.58,Italics,Eren,0,0,0,,I'm the older one...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.62,0:00:43.59,Italics,Eren,0,0,0,,I gotta keep it together.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.89,0:02:22.34,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Looks like you're doing a bit better, Saaya.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:22.34,0:02:25.47,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Sorry, Senpai. I'm fine now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.58,0:02:25.92,shopping,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs15\3c&HDDEDEA&\c&H5F6564&\move(381,334,381,197,21,2315)}Tokyo Metropolitan Police Hospital Front Entrance Station
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.92,0:02:28.08,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Today's area is Nakano Ward...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.08,0:02:31.04,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Yup. Good thing it's not far from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.46,0:02:34.58,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,We'll be sticking together today \Nso it's not as scary!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.80,0:02:40.65,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Let's get our revenge \Nand find those postboxes!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.65,0:02:41.44,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.58,0:03:06.29,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,700)\pos(330,60)\fs40\b1}Nakano Ward
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.29,0:03:07.58,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(650,1)\pos(330,60)\fs40\b1}Suginami Ward
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.91,0:03:13.34,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,A blue postbox!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.72,0:03:15.24,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,Kaido Senpai?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.73,0:03:17.24,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.44,0:03:21.57,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,Ugh... I can't see!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.68,0:03:28.15,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,It's probably too late \Nto submit something now...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.31,0:03:39.99,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Finally! A postbox!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.87,0:03:43.74,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,A guy? How are you alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.50,0:03:48.06,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Oh, well. It's not like there's cops anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.06,0:03:50.75,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,All I have to do is kill you \Nand submit my entry!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.09,0:03:54.17,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Who are you?! You gonna attack me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.17,0:03:56.14,Italics,Rika,0,0,0,,Who cares? Just ignore him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.28,0:04:01.44,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,I'm Rika Suzuki. \NOf course, I'm attacking you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.44,0:04:02.89,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Wait, why did I just—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.89,0:04:04.22,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I reject!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.22,0:04:07.48,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,What? You "reject"?! Whatever!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.48,0:04:10.85,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,I'm gonna kill you! And make it out alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.85,0:04:12.11,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,I missed?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.70,0:04:15.90,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Damn you, kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.45,0:04:19.16,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,What do I do with this?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.16,0:04:21.37,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,If I use it now, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.94,0:04:26.00,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Like worrying will do me any good!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.96,0:04:28.16,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.16,0:04:31.50,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,See ya! Hope you stay alive, Suzuki-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.42,0:04:40.43,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Tasers really come in handy \Nin times like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.22,0:04:43.97,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Weapons aren't about specs. \NIt's how you use them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.97,0:04:46.41,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Maybe you'll learn that later tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.18,0:04:49.81,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,First entry: no Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.81,0:04:51.39,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Second entry: with Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.39,0:04:54.06,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Five minutes from starting point \Nand ten minutes from execution point...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.16,0:04:56.73,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Oh, that reminds me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.69,0:05:02.36,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Now... Oh my, look at you. How unlucky.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.82,0:05:04.68,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,You must have cut an artery when you fell.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.68,0:05:06.96,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Maybe you shouldn't use \Nsteel pipes like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.45,0:05:10.21,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,You're the one who shot me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.21,0:05:14.36,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,At this rate, you'll die. What to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.36,0:05:15.42,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,You bitch!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.04,0:05:20.83,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Don't you want to live? I know how.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.77,0:05:23.43,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,I'm so sick of this!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.43,0:05:26.91,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,I bet these postboxes don't even exist! \NThere's no way we can beat the Emperor!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.91,0:05:29.01,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Everyone's destined to die!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.01,0:05:30.13,Italics,Saaya,0,0,0,,Eren Senpai...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.13,0:05:35.17,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,I can't do this anymore! \NI wanna go to my parents'...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.17,0:05:38.96,Italics,Saaya,0,0,0,,We're so helpless. \NWe can't even find a postbox.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.36,0:05:41.16,Italics,Saaya,0,0,0,,Sorry, Saneatsu...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.22,0:05:46.78,Emperor,Emperor,0,0,0,,It's time. We will now \Nbegin tallying the majority.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.78,0:05:47.79,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30\c&HFFFFEE&}As a result of Tasuketsu, I'm...\N- Alive or Dead
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.87,0:05:53.83,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30}As a result of Tasuketsu, I'm...\N- Alive or Dead
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.62,0:05:54.72,Emperor,Emperor,0,0,0,,We've passed midnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.26,0:05:59.39,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Could that mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.94,0:06:07.75,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Saneatsu! You really came back to life!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.22,0:06:10.10,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Huh? Back to life?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.23,0:06:12.42,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Saaya?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.79,0:06:14.36,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,I'm so weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.67,0:06:19.18,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,I was about to break our promise... \Nbut I'm okay now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.60,0:06:23.38,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,I remembered that I have nothing to be \Nscared about as long as I have our promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.38,0:06:24.71,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Saaya...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.71,0:06:27.76,Italics,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,When did the two of them get so close?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.41,0:06:32.37,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Senpai! I was dead, too! Hold me!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.37,0:06:34.00,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Go die again!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.35,0:06:37.58,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,We were all dead and then \Nbrought back to life?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.46,0:06:40.46,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Look! The lights!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.18,0:06:43.95,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Everyone who died from Tasuketsu was revived!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.69,0:06:49.39,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,W-Why?! Why would they come back to life?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.39,0:06:51.83,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,I could have gotten rid of men \Nonce and for all!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.83,0:06:55.03,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,I came all this way just \Nto see their dead bodies!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.03,0:06:57.62,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Too bad I'm the only one here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.22,0:07:00.86,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,Men are always this way...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.86,0:07:03.11,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,Just like my dad! \NJust like the guys in class!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.11,0:07:07.11,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,All men are nothing but power-hungry trash!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.11,0:07:10.19,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,Even smart ones like you! Even now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.19,0:07:12.12,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,It's proof that I'm right!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.12,0:07:13.12,Default,Kaido,0,0,0,,Go to hell!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.59,0:07:19.68,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,So Mika Kaido isn't the Emperor...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.07,0:07:21.50,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Then that means...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.25,0:07:26.51,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Is there no announcement \Non the next designated area tonight?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.24,0:07:30.97,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,So the revival did work... Mido, Iruga.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.03,0:07:34.66,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Thanks for the trouble, Isshiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.66,0:07:37.73,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Just like you said, Mido. \NThere was a male who was alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.73,0:07:42.22,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Short hair with an accent... in \Ngrade school or middle school.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.22,0:07:43.65,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,I figured...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.98,0:07:47.91,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Owner of the quasi-major \NPrime Right to Rejection!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.22,0:07:53.84,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,But he doesn't seem very bright. \NHe used his best idea this early in the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.84,0:07:56.63,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Isshiki, bring around the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.54,0:07:59.11,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,Roger that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.18,0:08:08.26,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Iruga, do you recognize the kid she mentioned?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.47,0:08:12.88,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,Nah. Nope, sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.88,0:08:16.49,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,You heard the lady. \NGrade school or middle school.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.88,0:08:20.66,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Fine. I guess it can wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.61,0:08:27.18,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Besides, how rude of Isshiki... \NCalling Tasuketsu a "game".
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.40,0:08:31.46,Default,Iruga,0,0,0,,She must be thinking \Nthe Emperor's just playing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.46,0:08:32.41,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Now...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.41,0:08:35.33,Default,Isshiki,0,0,0,,The fun's about to start...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.99,0:08:37.96,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,W-Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.08,0:08:40.54,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30}You are currently looking at this\Nscreen in Tokyo Prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.45,0:08:40.54,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Why is there another question?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.54,0:08:43.52,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,No... Then everyone who came back to life...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.52,0:08:44.75,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Could it be a Prime Right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.06,0:08:49.72,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,Shoot, they got me! This is \Nthe Prime Right to Re-execution!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.09,0:08:54.68,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,It was all someone's plan... \Nand they used my question?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.28,0:09:00.15,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,They must have done it to prevent \Nrevival of victims later on.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.69,0:09:03.06,Default,Male,0,0,0,,What are you kids yelling about \Nso late at night?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.29,0:09:06.92,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Look at the screen! Please, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.58,0:09:08.82,Default,Male,0,0,0,,The screen?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.94,0:09:14.03,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30}You are currently looking at this\Nscreen in Tokyo Prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.66,0:09:12.16,Emperor,Emperor,0,0,0,,We've passed 12:10AM.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.03,0:09:16.37,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,H-How?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.03,0:09:19.62,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,He was looking at the screen...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.75,0:09:23.17,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Idiots will just get in the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.17,0:09:26.63,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,The Emperor's motive isn't \Nto play a game, it's "recovery".
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.63,0:09:29.53,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,I don't need imbeciles who can't \Nunderstand something as simple as that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.85,0:09:34.00,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Say goodbye to hope... \NFinally, it begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.35,0:09:36.01,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30}You are currently looking at this\Nscreen in Tokyo Prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.01,0:09:41.06,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs22\c&HFFF9EF&\3c&HFFF9EF&\pos(40,91)}Prime Rights: 13 left\NRights: 47 left
Dialogue: 1,0:09:36.01,0:09:41.06,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFF9EF&\3c&HFFF9EF&\pos(320,77)}Today's Area
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.01,0:09:41.06,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(3000,1)\b1\c&HFFF9EF&\3c&HFFF9EF&\fs30\pos(322,234)}Nerima Ward
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.01,0:09:41.06,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an3\pos(597,303)\c&HFFF9EF&\3c&HFFF9EF&}2,215,466 people left
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.50,0:09:43.44,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,The Tasuketsu from two days ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.44,0:09:46.27,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,All the males died from that, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.27,0:09:48.48,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,How were we brought back to life?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.48,0:09:50.03,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Yesterday's question...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.03,0:09:53.77,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,"As a result of Tasuketsu, \NI'm 'alive' or 'dead'".
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.77,0:09:55.46,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,A deficit of the dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.46,0:10:00.70,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,As the majority, the dead were \Nmade "undead"... meaning alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.16,0:10:05.50,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Are the dead part of Tasuketsu? Can't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.50,0:10:08.18,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Besides, how could dead people \Ncome back to life?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.55,0:10:13.34,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,If you're gonna say that, how can people \Ndie from a simple tally in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.12,0:10:21.57,Italics,Omi,0,0,0,,It's my fault. If I hadn't used\Nthat question so soon...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.54,0:10:24.33,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Omi, what's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.62,0:10:27.58,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Narita-kun...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.58,0:10:29.15,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Call me Saneatsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.06,0:10:33.84,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,We're in this together now, aren't we?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.84,0:10:37.53,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,We're friends. No need to be formal.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.53,0:10:39.06,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Friends?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.72,0:10:42.83,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,S-Saneatsu...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.83,0:10:44.75,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Yeah, there we go!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.19,0:10:47.25,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Hey, Sensei?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.09,0:10:52.01,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Were you the informatics teacher \Nfor all the first-years?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.42,0:10:53.93,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Yeah, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.70,0:10:58.76,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Then can you tell me what kind \Nof students those kids are?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.76,0:11:04.79,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Sure, if you tell me more about you. \NI'm not too familiar since it's my first year.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.79,0:11:07.09,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Sure, we're a team now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.73,0:11:15.28,Label,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}Fujishiro, Saaya
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.25,0:11:09.79,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Fujishiro is from Class D.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.79,0:11:12.70,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Good grades, never in trouble. \NAn excellent student all around.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.14,0:11:15.28,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,She's even part of the Student Council.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.28,0:11:31.96,Label-small,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(170,1)\pos(545,351)}Fujishiro, Saaya
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.74,0:11:20.03,Label,Sign,0,0,0,,Narita, Saneatsu
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.04,0:11:20.03,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Narita is from Class A. Not the best \Nat studying, but he's pretty sharp.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.03,0:11:31.96,Label-small,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(170,1)\pos(92,351)}Narita, Saneatsu
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.49,0:11:26.54,Label,Sign,0,0,0,,Sato, Kazuhiko
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.86,0:11:22.08,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Sato's also from Class A.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.08,0:11:26.54,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,He's always loud in class, but \Nhe can make friends with anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.54,0:11:31.96,Label-small,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(170,1)\pos(92,181)}Sato, Kazuhiko
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.00,0:11:31.96,Label,Sign,0,0,0,,Jin, Omi
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.30,0:11:31.47,Default-Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Jin is from Class C. He usually \Nsits quietly alone in class.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.77,0:11:33.80,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,So?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.42,0:11:40.51,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I don't know what he was down about, \Nbut he did smile for the first time.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.40,0:11:43.43,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,You're a nice guy, Saneatsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.43,0:11:47.72,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,It's not like that. I just...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.72,0:11:56.11,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,When I was four, my mom and I were out \Nwhen a truck came and...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.74,0:12:02.57,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Somehow, I survived. \NBut by the time I woke up,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.98,0:12:06.12,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,my amazing mom was gone from this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.51,0:12:12.49,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,My dad's always overseas for work, \Nand I shut myself in my room.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.49,0:12:15.32,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I was starting to think \NI'd be better off dead when...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.59,0:12:22.94,Flashback,Younger Ryuta,0,0,0,,Hey! I just moved in next door. \NI'm Ryuta Ichinose!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.94,0:12:24.43,Flashback,Younger Ryuta,0,0,0,,Are you Narita-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.77,0:12:26.18,Flashback,Younger Ryuta,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.18,0:12:31.12,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,From then on, it didn't matter \Nif I agreed or what time it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.12,0:12:33.69,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,He always came barging in out of nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.08,0:12:39.61,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,But I found myself going along \Nwith Ryuta's antics... and enjoying it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.90,0:12:45.49,Flashback,Younger Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Hey, Ryuta... Why did you come talk to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.77,0:12:49.71,Flashback,Younger Ryuta,0,0,0,,Did you know? There's something \Nreal precious in this world!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.11,0:12:51.40,Flashback,Younger Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.40,0:12:54.29,Flashback,Younger Ryuta,0,0,0,,Parents, siblings, loved ones, \Nand best friends!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.94,0:12:59.26,Flashback,Younger Ryuta,0,0,0,,Now I have more of them! \NSince we're best friends!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.88,0:13:07.66,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I've made it my goal since then... to \Nhelp someone like Ryuta saved me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.66,0:13:10.10,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I wanna be a person who can save others.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.66,0:13:14.61,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,That's why helping someone \Nis actually for my own merit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.18,0:13:17.40,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I'm not some noble person.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.40,0:13:22.78,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Starting today, let's meet three times \Neach day in the afternoon, evening,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.78,0:13:25.08,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,and at night to share information more often.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.53,0:13:28.43,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It'll help us expand our search \Nand improve efficiency.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.02,0:13:34.42,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,If only there was another \Nhint besides postboxes...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.06,0:13:40.76,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I'm about to ask you a question. \NAnswer with "yes" or "no".
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.38,0:13:44.47,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Can you promise not to run or resist?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.83,0:13:47.93,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Y-Yes. I promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.93,0:13:49.09,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I have something to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.60,0:13:52.69,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I prefer speaking to Saaya Fujishiro, \Nbut it can't be helped.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.33,0:13:54.51,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Let's go somewhere else.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.81,0:14:00.07,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I've killed Mika Kaido.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.07,0:14:05.29,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I'll let you ask one question \Nbased on that information.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.29,0:14:07.19,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Don't say anything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.52,0:14:14.58,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Why do you rely so much on guns, Senpai?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.71,0:14:18.51,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,How did you arrive at that question?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.51,0:14:21.97,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I just assumed you killed her with a gun...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.37,0:14:24.59,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,but there's only so many bullets you can use.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.27,0:14:28.44,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,And you don't seem to have any \Nreservations about using them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.18,0:14:32.24,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You came up and actually spoke to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.81,0:14:38.69,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I assume that was to test \Nif I'm worth talking to.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.69,0:14:42.03,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,That goes to show how \Nimportant your matter is...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.03,0:14:43.43,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Fair enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.16,0:14:47.91,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,In fact, I'm glad you were the one \NI ran into, Saneatsu Narita.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.91,0:14:54.28,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,To be clear, Mika Kaido was the one who \Nkilled us with the "male or female" question.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.25,0:14:56.75,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,She was screaming about some nonsense,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.75,0:14:59.34,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,but she was too dangerous \Nto be roaming free, so I shot her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.34,0:15:01.28,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Kaido Senpai...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.72,0:15:04.05,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Before I tell you, I want to be sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.05,0:15:06.50,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Has the number of people \Nin your group changed?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.50,0:15:07.26,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.72,0:15:10.48,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Has anyone changed in their appearance?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.48,0:15:11.88,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.88,0:15:16.23,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Finally, who suggested running away \Nfrom school that day?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.85,0:15:18.31,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I think it was...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.23,0:15:20.04,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Get in!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.04,0:15:20.82,Flashback,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.36,0:15:24.40,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I see, that makes sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.78,0:15:30.01,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I suppose I was wrong... \Nbut I was also right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.10,0:15:34.20,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,At first, I presumed that \NOmi Jin was the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.20,0:15:35.43,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Omi?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.16,0:15:38.21,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,On the first day of Tasuketsu,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.21,0:15:41.12,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I didn't just acquire a gun. \NI acquired something else.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.75,0:15:42.00,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(750,1)\frz135\bord0\fax-0.35\pos(421,146)}Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.00,0:15:44.51,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The Prime Right of Obtainment.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.51,0:15:46.01,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,A Prime Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.82,0:15:52.06,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Precisely because I gained this strange \Npower, I became suspicious of Omi Jin.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.85,0:15:54.43,Flashback,Omi,0,0,0,,Are you gonna shoot me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.43,0:15:56.02,Flashback,Sudo,0,0,0,,Of course I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.02,0:15:57.39,Flashback,Omi,0,0,0,,I reject.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.84,0:16:00.79,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I found myself responding to a question \NI had no intention of answering.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.79,0:16:03.86,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,And the bullet I shot at point-blank \Nrange missed him completely.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.86,0:16:05.25,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,"I reject".
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.95,0:16:08.10,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,His right must be something \Nalong the lines of "Rejection".
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.36,0:16:07.36,OS,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Right of Rejection
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.62,0:16:11.37,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,As for forcing response of a question,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.82,0:16:15.25,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I suspect it's a right to "Response \NEnforcement" or something like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.24,0:16:13.99,OS,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Right of Response Enforcement
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.56,0:16:19.37,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Judging from the power balance of the two \Nabilities, Rejection must be a Prime Right,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.37,0:16:19.37,OS,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.37,0:16:21.92,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,and Response Enforcement must be a Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.63,0:16:21.63,OS,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Right
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.92,0:16:23.59,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Although their names aren't exact.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.94,0:16:25.14,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Omi?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.56,0:16:30.97,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I suspect he had a Prime Right and Right \Nbefore Tasuketsu even began.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.97,0:16:33.80,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,B-But he's not the Emperor, is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.80,0:16:36.91,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,That's not even the main concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.91,0:16:37.81,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.69,0:16:40.96,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,There's a traitor among your group.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.96,0:16:42.19,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,A traitor?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.19,0:16:46.80,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Who knows their motive, but \Nthere's damage already being done.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.80,0:16:49.52,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,They likely possess a Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.52,0:16:51.20,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You already know who it is?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.75,0:16:52.91,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I'm fairly sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.83,0:16:58.52,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Sudo Senpai, do you want \Nto rejoin the group?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.52,0:17:02.58,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I know you may have killed someone, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.58,0:17:06.14,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You were only acting rationally \Nso you could beat the Emperor...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.55,0:17:09.31,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I think we need you!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.59,0:17:14.53,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Thank you. A part of me \Nis saved by your words.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.53,0:17:19.33,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I'll answer a question in return. \NIs there anything you want to ask?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.58,0:17:28.14,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I guess... about your Prime Right and \Nyour theory on the revival last night?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.14,0:17:30.36,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I don't know about Rights,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.36,0:17:33.48,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,but Prime Rights will demand you take \Na risk when opening the envelope.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.36,0:17:33.99,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\frz135\bord0\fax-0.35\pos(421,146)}Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.98,0:17:37.79,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The risk involves... loss of a body part.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.99,0:17:34.12,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\frz135\bord0\fax-0.35\pos(421,146)\clip(m 403 80 l 358 97 449 218 523 186 506 187 437 118 418 148 394 120 408 95)}Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.12,0:17:34.37,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\frz135\bord0\fax-0.35\pos(421,146)\clip(m 400 155 l 449 218 523 186 506 187 435 117 410 141)}Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.37,0:17:34.87,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\frz135\bord0\fax-0.35\pos(421,146)\clip(m 417 150 l 460 198 490 180 440 128)}Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.79,0:17:40.29,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What?! Then—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.85,0:17:43.17,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I chose the scrotum.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.17,0:17:46.32,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,There's no need for reproductive \Nfunctions in this situation,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.32,0:17:47.92,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,and it's best to get rid of any vital points.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.84,0:17:52.05,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The Prime Right I gained is... Obtainment.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.55,0:17:52.05,OS,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Right of Obtainment
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.42,0:17:54.58,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Once I obtain a certain object,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.58,0:17:57.26,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I can maintain its number \Nand guarantee its availability.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.78,0:18:00.46,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,So your supply of bullets is...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.46,0:18:02.60,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Unlimited, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.56,0:18:08.83,Flashback,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Why do you rely so much on guns, Senpai?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.62,0:18:11.08,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,So that's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.08,0:18:14.54,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,As for the revival of the dead, \Nhow do you make sense of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.54,0:18:18.13,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Well, our theory is that "absence \Nof the dead" meant "undead"
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.13,0:18:20.67,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,which brought them back to life...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.39,0:18:24.46,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,But I think the condition of the deaths \Nbeing "as a result of Tasuketsu"
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.46,0:18:26.67,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,was the main key.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.07,0:18:30.93,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,It turned death on its head \Nby forcefully replacing the prerequisite
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.93,0:18:33.13,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,of directing questions \Nonly towards survivors.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.13,0:18:35.97,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You mean the person who \Nwrote the question knew?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.97,0:18:41.93,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Who knows? But I believe they \Nsubmitted it with good intentions.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.60,0:18:45.44,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Perhaps they truly just \Nwanted to revive the victims.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.56,0:18:47.81,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30}You are currently looking at this\Nscreen in Tokyo Prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.32,0:18:47.81,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The same can't be said \Nfor the second question.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.60,0:18:53.53,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I first assumed it was a plan devised \Nby the Emperor, in response to the revival.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.53,0:18:57.84,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,But if they were to intervene like that, \Nwhy not just kill people on their own?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.22,0:19:00.76,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,It's reasonable to conclude \Nthat someone used their Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.76,0:19:03.93,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,or Right to enforce a second question.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.33,0:19:05.83,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Someone else...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.22,0:19:08.27,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,If it's a matter of sabotaging \Nthe revival method,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.27,0:19:12.87,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,the most effective question is \N"You were just revived; Yes or No".
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.87,0:19:18.80,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,But if the revival doesn't work, the question \Nwould be directed towards survivors.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.19,0:19:22.28,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,This results in a unanimous "no". Game over.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.28,0:19:24.98,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The second question was likely submitted
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.98,0:19:29.18,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,by someone who couldn't determine \Nthe results of the first question.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.06,0:19:35.20,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,And to top it off, the Emperor's explanation \Nof the rules doesn't fit the reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.68,0:19:38.82,Emperor,Emperor,0,0,0,,The majority side \Nof the two answers will die.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.59,0:19:42.73,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,If they wanted to hide the revival method,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.73,0:19:45.46,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,why not just create a scheme \Nthat doesn't allow for them,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.46,0:19:47.72,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,or nullify those submissions?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.68,0:19:51.51,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,But they didn't do either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.01,0:19:58.00,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,This shows that the Emperor doesn't \Nhave a good grasp of Tasuketsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.17,0:20:01.41,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,If that's the case for the Emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.41,0:20:05.59,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,it's unlikely that the questioner recognized \Nthe loopholes behind the revival method.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.27,0:20:07.56,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Either they randomly came up with it,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.56,0:20:10.78,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,or they analyzed the situation like me \Nand found an answer...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.83,0:20:12.85,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.85,0:20:16.03,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Nothing, I'm just in awe...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.74,0:20:18.78,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Let's cut to the chase.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.67,0:20:23.08,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Be careful around Saaya Fujishiro.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.82,0:20:28.22,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Tasuketsu may be important, but the top \Npriority right now is eliminating the traitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.65,0:20:31.85,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Once it's too late, even submitting \Nquestions will be dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.26,0:20:33.71,Italics,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Saaya...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.15,0:20:37.48,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I'm about to tell you everything \NI've unraveled so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.48,0:20:39.89,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Listen carefully and use it \Nto your advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.90,0:20:43.20,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Senpai, thank y—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.20,0:20:46.30,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I chose the path to use force \Nagainst the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.67,0:20:49.69,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I don't want to drag you all \Ninto something so dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.26,0:20:51.46,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,About our talk...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.46,0:20:53.27,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I understand everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.27,0:20:56.32,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I'll become your sword \Nand defeat the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.06,0:21:00.65,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,In the meantime, go find postboxes \Nso you can continue surviving.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.65,0:21:01.65,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,For sure!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.29,0:21:04.87,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,What are you going to do \Nwhen you meet up with the group?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.20,0:21:10.32,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I have a plan. My strategy \Nand what to do next...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.12,0:21:16.10,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Is that so? I have faith in you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.92,0:21:19.92,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}Good Intentions
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.16,0:21:18.74,Default-Top,Sudo,0,0,0,,Good luck.
